  "title": "CIA Reading Room cia-rdp71b00529r000100090021-2: PROPOSED HEADQUARTERS EMPLOYEE BULLETIN #178, PICNIC TABLES AND BENCHES",
  "creator": "CIA Reading Room",
  "year": 1968,
  "subject": "CIA Reading Room",
  "description": "- GP ?J / Approved For Release 2000/05/05 : IA ,R QP710529R 09J -?~... ,.~. r! a. , ~\"' 3 jug1g63 m-/Z.I MEMORANDUM FOR: Executive Director-Comptroller Deputy Director for Science and Technology Deputy Director for Plans Deputy Director for Intelligence Inspector General General Counsel SUBJECT : Proposed Headquarters Employee Bulletin #178, Picnic Tables and Benches Forwarded for your information is attached subject proposal, which is being sent to the Deputy Director for Support for approval to publish. The Director of Logistics proposed publication of the bulletin to inform all employees of the newly placed picnic tables and benches and of the rules which must govern their use. If you have any questions.. regarding this proposal, please call me within two workdays on extension 2761. 25X1A Chief, Support Services Staff cc: D/L SSA-DDS CYJUN 1 Ercl i rd Nn a duiia;is Approved For Release 2000/05/099`: YdLWdF ' Bb0t29CO' 00090021-2 Approved For Release 2000/0 ADMINIST' I5/05 : CI V. - 7I,g0.9R000100090021-2 Headquarters EMPLOYEE BULLETIN #178 PICNIC TABLES AND BENCHES For your enjoyment during the lunch periods, picnic tables and benches have been placed on the lawn by the Headquarters Building cafeteria. To ensure your safety and provide an attractive eating area for everyone,-please observe the following rules: a. Do no cooking of any kind in the area. b. Take only paper plates and trays, not dishes and silverware, from the cafeteria to the picnic area. c. Clean up your table and the immediate area around it before leaving; return trays to the cafeteria. d. Do not smoke within 50 feet of the two large, green propane gas tank caps in the grass next to the cafeteria windows. ADMINISTRATIVE - INTERNAL USE ONLY Approved For Release 2000/05/05: CIA-RDP71 B00529R000100090021-2",
